# Sun Physics Model — SOTA Gap Analysis

> **Branch:** `sun-focus` (intentionally simplified to focus on Sun simulation)  
> **Audit date:** 2026-03-09  
> **Codebase total:** Backend ~1600 LOC, Frontend ~4100 LOC (9 modules + controller)

---

## Executive Summary

The current Sun physics model is **surprisingly deep for a real-time WebGL simulation** — already implementing several features that most Three.js solar visualizations lack entirely (Hathaway cycle forcing, real-time SWPC/SILSO data assimilation, Neckel-Labs limb darkening, RTV temperature scaling, Alfvén speed coupling). However, significant gaps remain versus state-of-the-art solar physics codes like COCONUT, AWSoM, and MAS.

**Maturity grade: Intermediate-Advanced (~60-70% of achievable fidelity for a real-time web simulation)**

The model excels at visual phenomena driven by observed scaling laws but lacks the underlying MHD physics that produces them. It's an "informed parametric model" rather than a physics solver.

