## Bottom Line

The model is **well above average** for a web-based solar visualization — it has genuine physics-based scaling laws, real-time data assimilation, and published observational coefficients throughout. The biggest gap to "hyper-fidelity" is **B1: data-driven PFSS from actual magnetograms**. This single feature would transform the model from "physically plausible parametric" to "observationally constrained" — making the coronal magnetic topology, coronal hole locations, and streamer belt geometry match reality for any given date.
